00:10:10.945 --> 00:10:12.450
It doesn't matter how strong you are.

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:15.120
She can use her relaxed and movement

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:17.604
to defend the big and strong opponent.

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:23.155
This is very classic there, elbow.

00:10:23.155 --> 00:10:24.540
And all this movement here,

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:28.080
this go into wooden dummy.

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:29.360
When you're watching a wooden dummy,

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:31.000
you're using a lot of this hand here,

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.107
elbow coming in, arm, turn,

00:10:33.107 --> 00:10:35.270
all this elbow stuff is all attack.

00:10:35.270 --> 00:10:38.020
So the body attack, elbow, elbow, elbow,

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:40.140
attacking, elbow defending all this.

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:42.832
Michelle Yeoh is very good at
demonstrating the movement.

00:10:42.832 --> 00:10:44.878
I will give this one 8 out of 10.

00:10:48.350 --> 00:10:50.170
This movement here you
can see, very classic.

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:52.943
Now, this is 6½-point-pole
training for the Wing Chun.

00:10:52.943 --> 00:10:55.200
One of the two weapon that Wing Chun use.

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:56.960
This is what the Wing Chun people use.

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:58.474
Instead of training on weight a lot,

00:10:58.474 --> 00:10:59.607
they're using that to train.

00:11:01.152 --> 00:11:03.470
They hold it like that because
they're using it for spear,

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:06.340
move, like whipping, twisting,

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:07.800
attacking, flicking.

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:09.780
There are only 6½ movements on this.

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:11.160
And they mix them up together

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:13.120
with the hand form and the footwork.

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:15.378
So the finger, the power onto the pole.

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:19.380
Is it really necessary,

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:21.550
two person using the same thing?

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:25.060
Now, reality term is two
person using same movement,

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:27.040
more likely both of them get cut up.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:28.880
This is the traditional Wing Chun side.

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:30.320
Butterfly knife and sword.

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:33.380
That's why Wing Chun use
long and short weapon.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:35.890
When the enemy have short weapon,

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:37.232
you're using long weapon.

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:41.190
A lot of the movement there,

00:11:41.190 --> 00:11:42.860
as you see the Wing Chun movement,

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:45.240
using hand movement,
like a hand attacking,

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:47.820
they transfer them into the weapon.

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:50.380
But onto the weapon for this to be used,

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:53.850
you're getting the idea of
illustrate the hand form.

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:55.200
And then now you got a weapon

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:56.710
attached to your body here,

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:59.169
so you can able to move well to using it.

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:02.461
OK, stop that there. That's part of, like,

00:12:02.461 --> 00:12:04.860
called a butterfly knife chi sao.

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:06.080
Instead of using hand,

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:07.610
they're using a knife instead.

00:12:07.610 --> 00:12:09.840
Controlling the force
coming in hard and soft.

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:11.293
See, the classic, what I told you about,

00:12:11.293 --> 00:12:12.870
in Wing Chun side, hard and soft.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.220
You're using to moving

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:15.718
your energy from your opponent there.

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:19.267
When it get close, the
weapon they can be using,

00:12:19.267 --> 00:12:20.241
use the elbow.

00:12:20.241 --> 00:12:22.700
And then they use a knife
when it got a distance,

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:24.191
because you're going to need a distance

00:12:24.191 --> 00:12:25.432
to be able to use it.

00:12:25.432 --> 00:12:26.650
When they're closing up,

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:29.390
that's when they use elbow, head, knee,

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:31.557
and also using shoulder a lot as well.

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:35.570
They're using the classic
chain punch coming in.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:37.903
Idea is, when you punch
somebody once, they block,

00:12:37.903 --> 00:12:39.049
but when you bam, bam, bam, bam,

00:12:39.049 --> 00:12:40.010
they can't block like this.

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:42.113
So more than likely, if I do 20 punch,

00:12:42.113 --> 00:12:43.900
they will land on your face once.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:45.030
What you're going to use to block it,

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:47.417
using either wing block or using pak sao

00:12:47.417 --> 00:12:49.226
to block of this chain punch.

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:53.950
Classic biu jee. Biu jee, finger strike.

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:56.508
Attacking the eye, attacking the throat,

00:12:56.508 --> 00:12:57.880
attacking a vulnerable spot.

00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:59.000
Emergency use.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.040
When you get to this level of biu jee,

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:03.290
you have become very
dangerous to your opponent.

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:05.800
So got to be very careful
how you're using it.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:07.266
Instead of see, he feel now.

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:10.956
Bruce Lee use a lot of 1-inch punch.

00:13:10.956 --> 00:13:12.510
Like that, boom, boom, boom!

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:14.410
When you attack, you feel them first,

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:17.730
then follow up onto second,
and then use your weight.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:19.980
But when you punch them
when they are tense, ooh!

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:22.610
Next movement, you hit
them, they start, ah!

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:25.150
When they start to, ah!
Then the last one, bang!

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:27.330
Then you're forcing the energy past it.

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:28.380
That's how you knock them out.

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:30.130
Overall, for choreography,

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:32.389
very, very good. The ways they do them,

00:13:32.389 --> 00:13:35.606
they showcase very truthfully
little bit of Wing Chun,

00:13:35.606 --> 00:13:37.960
how you use it on the scene.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:40.743
I give them about 8 to 9 out of 10.

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:45.003
This is all Wing Chun movement,

00:13:45.003 --> 00:13:46.670
the movement on there that he coming in.

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:47.730
Attacking, defending.

00:13:47.730 --> 00:13:49.860
But is it Wing Chun movement here?

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:51.640
Is it more traditional side?

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:53.255
No, more Wing Chun there

00:13:53.255 --> 00:13:55.690
start to fit into him going Jeet Kune Do.

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:57.260
That's why he use a lot of high kick.

00:13:57.260 --> 00:13:58.960
What Bruce Lee believing in,

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:01.860
what you take is useful;
reject what is useless.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:04.120
So he discard a lot of traditional stuff

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:05.395
that no functional to him.

00:14:06.571 --> 00:14:07.820
That's another classic one.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:10.110
This is the chum kiu
movement coming in arm break.

00:14:10.110 --> 00:14:11.690
Boom, arm break, coming in arm break.

00:14:11.690 --> 00:14:13.700
So that's what it is. Soon coming in hand

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:16.240
breaking the arm,
control, breaking the leg,

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:18.454
sidekick of the Wing
Chun low kick on there

00:14:18.454 --> 00:14:21.935
to hurting the joint
to the lower leg there.

00:14:21.935 --> 00:14:23.011
Very classic, yeah.

00:14:23.959 --> 00:14:25.460
What he trying to demonstrate there,

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:27.943
is in the Wing Chun side,
we fight in a closed ring.

00:14:27.943 --> 00:14:29.330
We don't need space,

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:31.500
but what Chuck Norris need, space,

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:32.620
because he use a lot of kick.

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:34.090
Bruce Lee, he don't need space.

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:35.170
Now when he get close,

00:14:35.170 --> 00:14:36.740
he don't use any of the high kick now.

00:14:36.740 --> 00:14:37.750
He using low kick.

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:40.508
I have to give this 10 out
of 10, because he's my idol.

00:14:43.108 --> 00:14:44.740
This is more like Kali,

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:46.800
Kali movement than more like Wing Chun.

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.277
But Wing Chun do that as well.

00:14:48.277 --> 00:14:49.790
You're using this to drill.

00:14:49.790 --> 00:14:53.270
This kind of drill is helping
you to get the sensitivity.

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:55.700
When you put that knife on the person,

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.833
you see how much power
they put into your arm,

00:14:57.833 --> 00:14:58.879
how you respond.

00:15:02.120 --> 00:15:02.953
Joe: Again.

00:15:02.953 --> 00:15:04.640
People need to understand,
a drill is a tool.

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:07.900
You need 1,000 repetition
to be able to respond.

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:09.820
You need to drill that into your system.

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:11.440
When something happen in real life,

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:12.590
fight, you can't think.

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:14.700
You either feel or see before it happen.

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:16.690
So the whole idea of learning this

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:17.790
is to learn about feel,

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:19.810
learn about see, where
you place your hand,

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:21.870
where you put your hand,
how you put your hand,

00:15:21.870 --> 00:15:23.820
because all the knife
and hand is very fast.

00:15:26.030 --> 00:15:26.880
Joe: Good.

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:28.860
This one here is not really attack.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:30.180
This is really like drill.

00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:31.590
When somebody put a knife at you,

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:32.930
two thing you need to realize.

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:35.863
If you're in a situation
that you got nowhere to go,

00:15:35.863 --> 00:15:37.740
you have to make sure
you're looking for weapon.

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:39.590
Make sure there's something you can use

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:40.940
to be able to defend that quickly.

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:43.740
Think fast, and looking
for the exit to run,

00:15:43.740 --> 00:15:44.600
to get out of the way.

00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:46.991
Don't stay in front of that,
because you cannot defend it.

00:15:46.991 --> 00:15:48.520
Know yourself, know your enemy,

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:50.030
know your ability, and
know your surrounding.

